{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And to set you on high</b> — a hint to tefillin, as the Holy One, blessed be He, regarding whom it is written: אשריך ישראל (your blessing, O Israel)." "<b>For praise and for a name and for glory</b> — that is, what Israel praises and lauds to HaShem becomes for them glory. And that is what we say: the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to be a crown on the head of each and every righteous person. For that crown with which they crown the Holy One, blessed be He, in their prayer — He returns to them. But whoever engages in idle conversation in the synagogue, his entire body is encompassed with thorns. Therefore Shir HaShirim is not. And corresponding to it: כקול הסירים (like the voice of thorns)." "<b>which He has made</b> — in gematria: the seventy nations." "<b>And to be</b> — defective vav. For the vitality of their holiness is not so apparent in this world." "<b>Holy</b> — defective yod. That is: sanctify yourself a little below, and they sanctify you above. And likewise four occurrences of קדוש ישראל in the Prophets." "<b>And to be a holy people</b> — and adjacent to it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The hint appears to turn on the word עליון ('on high') and its association with tefillin (טוטפות) via the verse cited, though the precise logic of the connection is terse.", 1 "The phrase 'therefore Shir HaShirim is not' is obscure; possibly meaning the Song of Songs does not apply to such a person, or the phrase is elliptical/corrupt. Read hyper-literally.", 4 "Resolved לו' as לומר ('that is'); the four-occurrence Masorah count of קדוש ישראל is in the Nevi'im (Prophets)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:52.788839857Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}